## THE TEXTS (ADF comments; build from the sources and freeze)
ASCII; `<<NAME>>` printed by program in the same action as the write; after the fill `<<` and `>>` count 0. **Jira comment texts, C-entry, BACKLOG and history text carry NO internal words: no person's name, no decision-card id, no B-number, no finding id, none of the words seat, brief, lane, gate, tuesday, live, deployed, complet (so "complete", "completed"); say "independent review" for a review and "the coordinator" for the coordinator seat; no dollar sign, percent sign, backtick, or digit-dot-digit (file:line pointers, shas and three-part versions exempt; other figures whole numbers); say `success` for a check-run.** The name scan is UNDERSCORE-AWARE: the pattern is `(?<![A-Za-z])<name>(?![a-z])` (or split on `_` first) for every name of the ban list (the product owner's and the reviewer's names, the staff names in the project's records, the coordinator seat names; build the list from the earlier STATUS files and say how), and its control plants `_by_<a ban-list name>_` and must fire. Exemptions by EXACT STRING only in the root records files (never in Jira): "Measured by this seat at write time", "this seat did not query the decision store", "Recorded by B1470 SEAT-R204", the row ids, "written by B1470". The Jira comments have none.
**TX-<key>** (one comment per key, a paragraph per label): `<<key>>: <<PR number>>, squash <<SQ8>>, merged <<AE>> (by program), an ancestor of code main <<MAIN8>>, re-read from the API on the write day. <<Moved to Done under the product owner's 1 November ruling that Done means merged to main | Recorded; not moved: <<the named unmet clause or the condition that holds it>>>>.` Then the Done-when clauses, one row each, MET | NOT MET | NOT RE-DERIVED, with the pointer. Then `Open:` what holds the ticket and who can release it (omit when moved). Then the rule line: `Done rule: the product owner's 1 November ruling, in this project's records: "Done means merged to main, the same as Composer"; a ticket moves only where every Done-when clause is met and no review line or red run stands against it (the coordinator's reading).` Then `The squash is merged to main only; it is not in any hosted build (relayed, not probed by this pass).` Then `Source: records pass, <<DAY>>.` For a tier B key with no PR, replace the first paragraph by what the independent review or the lane's measurement showed (facts, with the file and line), "no change was needed on main" or "not built, held by <<the ruling>>". No sentence is drafted for the product.

